{
  "title": "The Twenty-Fifth of Dhul Hijjah",
  "data": "Imitate the Ahl al-Bayt (a.s.) in their three days of fasting: observe fasting, give alms to the poor and the orphans (especially at the twenty-fifth night of Zilhajj) and do your best to offer food to the needy.\nSay [al-Ziyarah al-Jaame’ah](G13) and [Dua al-Mubaahalah](AC21). In the view of some scholars, the twenty-fifth of Zilhajj is the Day of Mubaahalah.",
  "merits": "On this blessed day, [Surah al-Dahr](A80) (or al-Insan No. 76) was revealed praising the Ahl al-Bayt (a.s.) for they had observed fasting for three days and given their food to a poor, an orphan, and a captive for three days respectively. All over these three days, they used to break their fasting with water only."
}
